# Independent CI candidate gate review

Reviewed candidate.py/test_candidate.py on base 70f2d7e against spec15 same-artifact/freshness and CI gate requirements, current ci.yml job names and official workflow-run/jobs REST contracts. No implementation edits or live API mutations.

No blocking finding in this offline run/check boundary. Repository and head-repository IDs/names, selected workflow path/ID, run/attempt, main branch/source and successful completion are bound to caller pins. Required 8 job names match current ci.yml. Every listed job must share run/attempt/source, job IDs cannot repeat, required names cannot repeat, and all required jobs must complete successfully. A count exactly matching the supplied list with at most 100 entries rejects partial pagination; the caller must acquire an authenticated complete attempt-specific response.

Independent 4-test suites passed normally and under python -O. Additional tests confirmed 100 jobs accepted, 101 rejected, and boolean/float total_count rejected. The saved actual run 34700590547 and jobs response verified successfully with source bd74af3153fccd879d5363fa1b0d32db40be8044, attempt 1. For that interoperability probe current_main was taken from the saved run, so this is not a claim that it is the current main or an eligible deployment today. Response hashes and outcomes are retained.

This gate does not fetch or authenticate responses, prove an artifact's upload attempt, obtain/pin fresh main immediately before mutation, enforce permissions/lock, or authorize publication. A Candidate returned from these observations is not T16/runtime/Web acceptance and does not turn historical CI into current public/LKG proof. Parent full-suite runs predating this module do not validate the new module.

Official sources accessed 2026-09-13:
- https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-runs#get-a-workflow-run
- https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-jobs#list-jobs-for-a-workflow-run-attempt
The jobs endpoint selects run and attempt and supports per_page up to 100. Larger workflows require a separately specified complete-pagination contract; this implementation conservatively rejects them.

Final revision review: all optional jobs must also be completed with success/skipped; independent queued, in_progress and cancelled optional probes reject, while skipped delivery passes. Final 5-test suites pass normally and under python -O; earlier 4-test logs remain historical. Final tools/site/README.md accurately separates candidate checks from authenticated fetch, attempt-bound artifact provenance and mutation permission.
